<http://data.silknow.org/object/84678f33-9a05-31a5-a654-9479a066718a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Worked on the sampler are the alphabet, numbers, flowers, a parrot, a squirrel, the date 1765 and rectangular spaces filled with various canvas work stitches.  A monogram surmounted by a crown are worked with gold thread and pink and light blue silk.  The edge is buttonholed in scallops. Stitches: couching, counted satin, cross, eyelet, French knot, long-armed cross, rice, rococo, tent, two-sided Italian cross,"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/0d857ced-04b0-3d20-afc8-e006d5be4cfd> ;
